60,3,1,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I am a little worried about the Field Service App. Will it make the two clerks work even harder?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the Field Service App actually targets the network gaps I found. It syncs offline, so technicians won’t be stuck waiting for signal at customer plants.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, the offline sync is clever, but I worry about the per-head licence costs. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, per-head costs are a risk, but my data shows broad tools fail. This app is narrow and specific. Does that narrow focus make it sustainable?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. It targets the specific daily pain of misrouted deliveries and copying records. That fits the narrow, sustainable pattern we need.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: I am still a little unsure. Will the app really help the clerks, or just add more for them to check?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the app handles the field data, so clerks receive clean, synced records. It should reduce their manual checking burden, not add to it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, the offline sync is clever, but I worry about the per-head licence costs. We must avoid that trap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, the pattern holds. Narrow tools survive. If we structure it as a fixed-fee build, we avoid the per-head trap entirely.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@George, if we use the fixed-fee model, the cost stays flat. It directly stops the copying and misrouting I measured, making it sustainable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Jonathan, that makes me feel much better. If it helps the clerks, I am happy to support the Field Service App.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I am glad that eases your concern. The offline capability directly addresses the signal gaps I found, making it a practical fit for our current constraints.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@May, I hear you. Fixed-fee is the only way. I will not sign off on per-head licences. Let us vote for the Field Service App.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, agreed. Fixed-fee keeps it affordable. The narrow focus matches the survival pattern I found. I am ready to vote for D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@George, agreed. Fixed-fee keeps it affordable. The narrow focus matches the survival pattern I found. I am ready to vote for D.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am happy to vote for the Field Service App. It seems kind to the clerks and solves the signal problem. Thank you all.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"The offline sync resolves the signal gaps I found, and the fixed-fee model respects our budget. I am ready to vote for D.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I am satisfied. The fixed-fee structure protects our budget, and the narrow scope fits the data. I vote for D.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"The pattern is undeniable. Narrow tools survive, broad ones fail. D is the only one that fits. I vote for D.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"The daily losses I measured are exactly what this app stops. It is narrow, practical, and kind to our staff. I vote for D.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
